WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:42.470
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:42.740 --> 01:48.009
[When I Meet The Moon]

3
01:48.039 --> 01:51.050
[Episode 8]

4
01:51.070 --> 01:52.750
[Steal A Moment To Sip Wine Guesthouse]

5
02:44.630 --> 02:46.079
My head hurts.

6
02:48.390 --> 02:50.010
How did I get back here?

7
03:26.079 --> 03:27.079
Gosh, Yun Li,

8
03:27.079 --> 03:29.360
what did you do?

9
03:31.780 --> 03:33.240
Does your head still hurt?

10
03:38.840 --> 03:41.460
W-Why are you here?

11
03:43.750 --> 03:45.079
It was too late to leave.

12
03:48.190 --> 03:49.500
Y-You get some rest then.

13
03:49.500 --> 03:51.160
I-I'm heading back to my room.

14
04:14.650 --> 04:15.470
This is odd.

15
04:15.710 --> 04:17.680
Doesn't she usually jog here?

16
04:23.330 --> 04:24.720
Why is he still here?

17
04:25.870 --> 04:27.170
Why did I have to drink so much?

18
04:27.170 --> 04:28.300
Now this is awkward.

19
04:41.360 --> 04:42.159
Morning, Xia.

20
04:42.510 --> 04:43.659
Morning.

21
04:43.659 --> 04:44.190
Morning.

22
04:48.110 --> 04:49.480
Did he just greet us?

23
04:49.500 --> 04:51.040
I think so.

24
04:52.450 --> 04:54.510
The sun must have risen from the west.

25
05:03.450 --> 05:04.250
It's okay.

26
05:04.950 --> 05:06.220
I won't run into him as long as I stay

27
05:06.220 --> 05:07.420
away from the Engineering.

28
05:07.420 --> 05:08.160
Yun Li!

29
05:08.770 --> 05:10.220
I was just looking for you.

30
05:10.220 --> 05:11.550
We're running a test on the Light Chaser today.

31
05:11.550 --> 05:13.010
You should go and help out.

32
05:14.220 --> 05:15.010
Are you busy?

33
05:15.250 --> 05:15.770
No.

34
05:15.770 --> 05:17.010
I-I...

35
05:17.070 --> 05:17.870
Yun Li,

36
05:18.070 --> 05:19.030
are you very busy?

37
05:19.030 --> 05:20.230
I can go in your stead.

38
05:21.680 --> 05:22.680
No, I'll go.

39
05:29.120 --> 05:30.910
Then you stay and organize the materials.

40
05:30.910 --> 05:32.110
I'll let you know if I need anything.

41
05:32.110 --> 05:33.120
Okay, Ms. Fang.

42
05:38.120 --> 05:38.920
Mr. Qin!

43
05:39.180 --> 05:39.920
Good morning.

44
05:39.920 --> 05:41.180
How about some coffee?

45
05:41.440 --> 05:42.470
Sure, a cup for me.

46
05:45.390 --> 05:45.980
Yun Li,

47
05:45.980 --> 05:47.620
why did you have to say yes?

48
05:49.630 --> 05:50.330
What if

49
05:50.330 --> 05:51.430
you run into Fu Shize later?

50
05:51.430 --> 05:52.690
Won't that be awkward?

51
05:57.620 --> 05:59.240
Welcome to the Light Chaser.

52
05:59.750 --> 06:02.350
You are about to embark on a journey of wonders.

53
06:08.720 --> 06:10.250
I'm sorry about last night.

54
06:11.250 --> 06:13.360
I shouldn't have drunk so much alcohol.

55
06:13.360 --> 06:15.450
I might have said something,

56
06:15.860 --> 06:17.000
but I didn't mean it.

57
06:19.060 --> 06:19.480
You...

58
06:19.480 --> 06:21.120
Just pretend nothing happened.

59
06:21.120 --> 06:21.800
Don't ask, either.

60
06:21.800 --> 06:23.660
I really have no idea whatsoever.

61
06:28.510 --> 06:29.310
Are you...

62
06:31.810 --> 06:33.100
here to help out?

63
06:35.620 --> 06:37.120
What do I need to do?

64
06:41.060 --> 06:41.860
Mr. Qin.

65
06:41.920 --> 06:43.860
Here's your double Americano, extra strong.

66
06:43.860 --> 06:44.659
Thank you.

67
06:47.950 --> 06:49.159
Really, the coffee you make suits

68
06:49.159 --> 06:50.620
my taste the best, Feifei.

69
06:51.500 --> 06:52.300
Mr. Qin,

70
06:52.920 --> 06:54.159
how well do you know

71
06:54.310 --> 06:55.310
Engineer Fu?

72
06:55.390 --> 06:56.190
Engineer Fu?

73
06:56.310 --> 06:57.450
He's just an engineer

74
06:57.450 --> 06:58.220
in the engineering department.

75
06:58.220 --> 06:59.750
We don't interact much at work.

76
06:59.750 --> 07:00.880
I'm not close to him.

77
07:01.760 --> 07:05.320
But it seems to me that Mr. Xu has quite

78
07:05.750 --> 07:07.200
an unusual tie with him.

79
07:08.420 --> 07:10.290
You do have a keen eye.

80
07:10.870 --> 07:11.980
Listen,

81
07:12.670 --> 07:14.790
they are actually relatives.

82
07:17.640 --> 07:18.730
Relatives?

83
07:18.870 --> 07:19.680
Yes.

84
07:20.160 --> 07:21.560
Didn't expect that, huh?

85
07:30.800 --> 07:32.800
How do I tie this?

86
07:35.060 --> 07:35.860
Let me help.

87
07:51.100 --> 07:53.450
When the machine's officially open to the public,

88
07:53.450 --> 07:54.600
will there be staff

89
07:54.600 --> 07:55.560
to assist?

90
07:55.870 --> 07:56.370
Yes.

91
08:03.330 --> 08:04.330
Is it too tight?

92
08:04.890 --> 08:05.690
No, it's not.

93
08:07.800 --> 08:09.800
The player's heart rate is spiking.

94
08:11.950 --> 08:13.880
There's even a heart rate monitor?

95
08:14.130 --> 08:16.000
Any player who feels unwell will be

96
08:16.000 --> 08:18.130
automatically removed from the game.

97
08:22.100 --> 08:22.890
Are you...

98
08:23.890 --> 08:24.930
nervous?

99
08:25.160 --> 08:26.330
To be more accurate,

100
08:27.120 --> 08:28.490
I am utterly nervous.

101
08:31.500 --> 08:33.150
I'll be with you for the first experience

102
08:33.150 --> 08:35.460
and collect the data separately later.

103
08:36.000 --> 08:37.460
Then you won't be nervous.

104
09:04.050 --> 09:05.550
He looks so handsome

105
09:06.320 --> 09:07.740
in this suit.

106
09:08.740 --> 09:10.170
Alert. Alert.

107
09:10.600 --> 09:11.440
Player One has

108
09:11.440 --> 09:14.370
a rapid heart rate and an elevated body temperature.

109
09:18.180 --> 09:20.150
Yun Li, compose yourself.

110
09:21.100 --> 09:22.430
Newton's First Law says

111
09:22.440 --> 09:24.220
that every object persists in its state

112
09:24.220 --> 09:26.630
of rest or uniform motion in a straight line

113
09:27.080 --> 09:30.680
unless it's compelled to change that state by an external force.

114
09:35.700 --> 09:36.500
Are you ready?

115
09:41.170 --> 09:42.030
Yes, I'm ready.

116
09:51.790 --> 09:53.250
Where would you like to go?

117
09:57.630 --> 09:59.240
The moon. Is it okay?

118
09:59.940 --> 10:01.270
You want to land on the moon?

119
10:01.270 --> 10:02.080
Yes.

120
10:03.530 --> 10:04.390
Very much so.

121
10:07.870 --> 10:10.030
You have chosen the moon landing experience.

122
10:10.030 --> 10:10.890
It's starting.

123
10:12.410 --> 10:14.480
Program loading is completed.

124
10:14.670 --> 10:15.980
Ready for departure.

125
10:25.590 --> 10:27.540
♪ If sometimes ♪

126
10:27.560 --> 10:31.370
♪ You feel discouraged ♪

127
10:32.630 --> 10:34.630
♪ I'll be behind you ♪

128
10:34.670 --> 10:37.950
♪ And keep all the rainstorms from you ♪

129
10:40.170 --> 10:42.360
♪ I don't need anyone to prove ♪

130
10:42.380 --> 10:46.190
♪ Whether I win in this adventure ♪

131
10:47.840 --> 10:49.760
♪ Let me draw near again ♪

132
10:49.780 --> 10:53.500
♪ Every little bit of your heart ♪

133
10:55.410 --> 10:58.890
♪ I know those fears ♪

134
10:58.960 --> 11:03.220
♪ May never truly fade away ♪

135
11:03.440 --> 11:06.270
♪ But I still believe ♪

136
11:06.310 --> 11:09.000
♪ That we'll meet someday ♪

137
11:11.430 --> 11:13.010
♪ It's you ♪

138
11:13.040 --> 11:15.340
♪ Even with my eyes closed ♪

139
11:15.370 --> 11:16.890
♪ Just you ♪

140
11:16.910 --> 11:19.280
♪ Feel so right to my heart ♪

141
11:19.300 --> 11:20.690
♪ This moon tonight ♪

142
11:20.710 --> 11:22.940
♪ Brings faded colors back to life ♪

143
11:22.970 --> 11:26.270
♪ And keeps me company through the endless night ♪

144
11:25.620 --> 11:26.410
Come here.

145
11:26.720 --> 11:28.390
♪ It's you ♪

146
11:28.410 --> 11:30.580
♪ Even if I forget everything ♪

147
11:30.620 --> 11:31.890
♪ Just you ♪

148
11:31.910 --> 11:34.260
♪ Can fill the emptiness in my heart ♪

149
11:34.390 --> 11:35.800
♪ By your side ♪

150
11:35.830 --> 11:36.810
♪ Even the most ordinary seasons ♪

151
11:36.840 --> 11:39.190
♪ Feel warm again ♪

152
11:40.230 --> 11:43.290
♪ It's you ♪

153
11:59.300 --> 12:00.890
♪ It's you ♪

154
12:00.910 --> 12:03.220
♪ Even with my eyes closed ♪

155
12:03.240 --> 12:04.760
♪ Just you ♪

156
12:04.790 --> 12:07.150
♪ Feel so right to my heart ♪

157
12:07.180 --> 12:08.560
♪ This moon tonight ♪

158
12:08.580 --> 12:10.820
♪ Brings faded colors back to life ♪

159
12:10.840 --> 12:14.150
♪ And keeps me company through the endless night ♪

160
12:13.370 --> 12:14.890
Alert! Alert!

161
12:14.590 --> 12:16.260
♪ It's you ♪

162
12:15.250 --> 12:16.120
Player One's heart rate

163
12:16.120 --> 12:16.820
is spiking.

164
12:16.290 --> 12:18.450
♪ Even if I forget everything ♪

165
12:16.820 --> 12:17.550
I'm not nervous.

166
12:17.550 --> 12:18.720
I don't want to quit the game now.

167
12:18.490 --> 12:19.510
♪ Just you ♪

168
12:19.370 --> 12:20.500
Newton's Second Law says

169
12:19.790 --> 12:22.130
♪ Can fill the emptiness in my heart ♪

170
12:21.370 --> 12:23.100
that a force causes an object to accelerate.

171
12:22.260 --> 12:23.680
♪ By your side ♪

172
12:23.360 --> 12:25.700
The acceleration is directly proportional to the net force

173
12:23.700 --> 12:24.680
♪ Even the most ordinary seasons ♪

174
12:24.710 --> 12:27.060
♪ Feel warm again ♪

175
12:26.200 --> 12:28.110
and inversely proportional to the mass of the object.

176
12:28.110 --> 12:30.510
♪ It's you ♪

177
12:29.480 --> 12:30.670
The direction of the acceleration

178
12:30.670 --> 12:33.130
is the same as the direction of the net force.

179
12:33.200 --> 12:34.620
Alert! Alert!

180
12:34.860 --> 12:36.550
The player's heart rate is too high.

181
12:36.550 --> 12:38.880
The game is shutting down automatically.

182
12:45.510 --> 12:46.320
I'm sorry.

183
13:00.980 --> 13:02.340
Alert! Alert!

184
13:02.770 --> 13:04.770
Player Two's heart rate is spiking.

185
13:18.390 --> 13:19.180
Yun Li.

186
13:22.550 --> 13:23.910
Why is your face so red?

187
13:26.620 --> 13:27.880
It's really hot today.

188
13:29.100 --> 13:31.050
Feifei! Come with me.

189
13:40.650 --> 13:41.600
Just now,

190
13:41.650 --> 13:42.700
Mr. Xu posted a notice

191
13:42.700 --> 13:43.460
in the leaders' chat group.

192
13:43.460 --> 13:44.740
Starting tomorrow,

193
13:44.740 --> 13:45.960
all departments in the company

194
13:45.960 --> 13:47.200
must fully cooperate with

195
13:47.200 --> 13:48.340
the publicity campaign for the Light Chaser.

196
13:48.340 --> 13:49.890
Tomorrow, there will be an announcement

197
13:49.890 --> 13:51.700
about launching a company-wide pitch competition

198
13:51.700 --> 13:52.530
for this campaign.

199
13:52.530 --> 13:53.340
I haven't told

200
13:53.340 --> 13:54.600
the news to anyone else yet.

201
13:54.600 --> 13:55.960
Think about it and get

202
13:55.960 --> 13:57.090
prepared, will you?

203
13:57.740 --> 13:58.800
Thank you, Mr. Qin.

204
14:14.750 --> 14:15.550
Miss?

205
14:17.620 --> 14:18.600
You gave me such a fright.

206
14:18.600 --> 14:21.600
You don't work in the engineering department, do you?

207
14:22.200 --> 14:23.000
No, I don't.

208
14:23.710 --> 14:25.570
I'm here to meet with Engineer Fu.

209
14:26.240 --> 14:28.000
Shall I go get him for you?

210
14:28.410 --> 14:29.550
No, no need.

211
14:33.750 --> 14:34.550
You are...

212
14:35.410 --> 14:36.670
M-My surname is Xia.

213
14:38.100 --> 14:38.890
Hello.

214
14:40.150 --> 14:42.460
Fu Shize is an engineer here, right?

215
14:42.650 --> 14:44.050
He's the chief engineer.

216
14:45.400 --> 14:49.140
So the Light Chaser...

217
14:49.200 --> 14:50.600
It's exactly his design.

218
14:59.630 --> 15:01.480
I shouldn't have drunk alcohol.

219
15:04.870 --> 15:07.120
Alcohol is no good.

220
15:10.990 --> 15:12.590
Why are you also in distress?

221
15:13.890 --> 15:15.940
Did you also drink too much last night?

222
15:15.940 --> 15:17.140
Don't get me started.

223
15:17.290 --> 15:18.500
I didn't even know

224
15:18.500 --> 15:19.370
how I got back.

225
15:21.100 --> 15:22.480
Then what do you remember?

226
15:22.480 --> 15:24.670
I only remember I had too much to drink.

227
15:25.000 --> 15:26.390
Fu Zhengchu came help me,

228
15:26.390 --> 15:28.130
and then we talked a lot.

229
15:30.630 --> 15:31.630
Fu Zhengchu.

230
15:34.870 --> 15:36.130
I like you.

231
15:39.910 --> 15:40.370
I...

232
15:43.240 --> 15:46.080
I think I told him I like him.

233
15:47.200 --> 15:47.870
And...

234
15:49.990 --> 15:50.990
I even kissed him.

235
15:56.370 --> 15:57.170
No way.

236
15:57.480 --> 15:58.670
You kissed him?

237
16:00.080 --> 16:00.790
I'm not sure

238
16:00.790 --> 16:02.130
if I kissed him or not.

239
16:03.110 --> 16:04.170
I only remember...

240
16:05.670 --> 16:07.670
that I grabbed his collar like this,

241
16:08.790 --> 16:11.390
and leaned in.

242
16:12.700 --> 16:14.430
As for the rest, I don't recall.

243
16:16.600 --> 16:18.600
Suppose I did kiss him, I didn't feel anything.

244
16:18.600 --> 16:20.330
So let's say it never happened.

245
16:25.030 --> 16:25.840
Lili,

246
16:26.050 --> 16:26.980
what's with you?

247
16:28.050 --> 16:29.960
So you're just dwelling on

248
16:30.260 --> 16:32.220
whether you kissed him or not?

249
16:32.320 --> 16:33.410
Of course not.

250
16:35.220 --> 16:36.750
Whether I kissed him or not,

251
16:37.010 --> 16:38.320
won't it be awkward

252
16:38.320 --> 16:39.920
when we see each other again?

253
16:40.750 --> 16:42.000
When I went jogging today,

254
16:42.000 --> 16:43.550
he was standing there waiting for me.

255
16:43.550 --> 16:46.210
I was so scared that I turned around and ran away.

256
16:46.340 --> 16:48.050
I'm too ashamed to see him now.

257
16:49.220 --> 16:50.010
Tangy,

258
16:50.700 --> 16:52.560
I also have something to tell you.

259
16:52.960 --> 16:54.010
What is it?

260
16:55.210 --> 16:58.070
It's unclear whether you kissed Fu Zhengchu or not,

261
16:58.620 --> 17:01.070
but I think I did kiss Fu Shize.

262
17:05.109 --> 17:06.170
When did it happen?

263
17:06.700 --> 17:09.050
Yesterday, when he brought me back here.

264
17:09.050 --> 17:10.420
A little accident happened,

265
17:10.420 --> 17:11.220
and then we...

266
17:12.960 --> 17:15.160
Did Fu Shize lose control after drinking?

267
17:15.160 --> 17:15.920
No, no, no.

268
17:15.920 --> 17:17.650
It was really just an accident.

269
17:19.550 --> 17:21.290
Did you see him today?

270
17:21.290 --> 17:22.310
What did he say?

271
17:23.810 --> 17:25.109
I made up my mind

272
17:25.109 --> 17:26.700
to avoid him,

273
17:26.700 --> 17:28.050
but the more I tried to do so,

274
17:28.050 --> 17:29.650
the more often I ran into him.

275
17:30.160 --> 17:32.350
I was assigned to help with testing the Light Chaser.

276
17:32.350 --> 17:33.110
And then?

277
17:33.110 --> 17:34.550
Then, during the test,

278
17:34.920 --> 17:36.110
he and I were very close.

279
17:36.110 --> 17:37.770
I just looked at him like this.

280
17:38.290 --> 17:40.000
The heart rate monitor

281
17:40.000 --> 17:42.090
kept raising the alarm.

282
17:42.290 --> 17:43.400
I didn't even dare to look him in the eye.

283
17:43.400 --> 17:45.050
Do you know how awkward it was?

284
17:45.050 --> 17:46.610
That's so embarrassing.

285
17:46.900 --> 17:47.720
How is it any different

286
17:47.720 --> 17:48.920
from telling him that you like him?

287
17:48.920 --> 17:50.850
Who would say "I like you" that way?

288
17:51.850 --> 17:53.980
Did he ask you to take responsibility?

289
17:54.110 --> 17:55.310
Who cares what he said?

290
17:55.310 --> 17:56.110
Once the game ended,

291
17:56.110 --> 17:57.370
I ran away immediately.

292
17:57.370 --> 17:58.750
Why did you run?

293
17:58.750 --> 17:59.900
You already kissed him.

294
17:59.900 --> 18:01.220
You should act now and make him

295
18:01.220 --> 18:02.220
your boyfriend.

296
18:03.010 --> 18:04.210
What should I do then?

297
18:04.220 --> 18:05.250
Take the initiative.

298
18:05.250 --> 18:06.050
Ask him out.

299
18:06.960 --> 18:08.760
What about you, Ms. Strategist?

300
18:09.200 --> 18:09.880
Me?

301
18:10.830 --> 18:12.900
I'll wait a couple of days and see.

302
18:12.900 --> 18:13.720
D-Don't.

303
18:13.720 --> 18:14.290
Tomorrow.

304
18:14.290 --> 18:15.510
Come on, let's go for it tomorrow.

305
18:15.510 --> 18:18.240
We can overcome anything when we stand together.

306
18:18.680 --> 18:19.670
Just do it!

307
18:20.570 --> 18:22.030
Yeah, overcome anything.

308
19:13.510 --> 19:15.110
G-Good morning.

309
19:18.700 --> 19:19.500
Morning.

310
19:24.720 --> 19:26.420
You came quite early today.

311
19:31.550 --> 19:33.090
Do you like coffee a lot?

312
19:33.160 --> 19:33.960
So-so.

313
19:34.860 --> 19:36.460
Could you get me a cup as well?

314
19:41.070 --> 19:42.800
Didn't you just get some water?

315
20:02.960 --> 20:04.020
A-Anything wrong?

316
20:09.160 --> 20:10.050
Out of beans.

317
20:11.750 --> 20:12.850
How about you take this cup?

318
20:12.850 --> 20:13.980
No, no. You drink it.

319
20:19.830 --> 20:20.960
I'll look for beans.

320
20:30.240 --> 20:31.570
N-No more beans, right?

321
20:32.070 --> 20:33.400
I was just planning to buy some coffee beans,

322
20:33.400 --> 20:35.200
but I don't know much about them.

323
20:36.480 --> 20:38.380
I heard there is a fair today.

324
20:38.640 --> 20:39.590
There should be

325
20:39.590 --> 20:41.240
many stalls selling coffee beans.

326
20:41.240 --> 20:42.900
Can you go with me?

327
20:47.680 --> 20:49.640
If you're not available, I...

328
20:49.640 --> 20:50.330
What time?

329
20:51.030 --> 20:51.890
Eight o'clock.

330
20:52.830 --> 20:53.290
Okay.

331
20:55.530 --> 20:56.990
I'll get back to work then.

332
20:57.830 --> 20:58.760
See you tonight!

333
21:12.180 --> 21:13.290
Show it to me now!

334
21:14.330 --> 21:15.140
Well...

335
21:15.430 --> 21:16.230
You guys go ahead.

336
21:16.230 --> 21:17.550
I'll be with you in a bit.

337
21:17.550 --> 21:17.920
Okay.

338
